# TradeBeginner Test Benchmarks

This file defines the benchmark contract for the full test program (Prompts 0-11).
It is the source of truth for what to test, how success is measured, and how failures
must be diagnosed.

## 1) Global Benchmark Contract

### 1.1 Required failure diagnostics
Every failed assertion must include:
- function under test
- failing input
- expected output/behavior
- actual output/behavior
- diagnosis category

Diagnosis categories (canonical):
- SAFETY_CRITICAL_DEFAULT
- TYPE_COERCION_FAILURE
- MISSING_VALIDATOR
- CONSTRAINT_NOT_ENFORCED
- SERIALIZATION_FAILURE
- MUTABLE_DEFAULT_SHARED
- ENUM_MISMATCH
- MISSING_ERROR_HANDLING
- RACE_CONDITION
- DATA_INTEGRITY
- SILENT_FAILURE
- WRONG_CALCULATION
- STATE_LEAKAGE
- MISSING_FEATURE
- PERFORMANCE
- API_CONTRACT

### 1.2 Mandatory docstring tag
Each test function must include:
- `FUNCTION TESTED: <module>.<symbol>`

### 1.3 Benchmark result model
Every benchmarked test run reports:
- Test Name
- Function Tested
- Result (PASS/FAIL/WARN)
- Problem Location
- Technical Issue

### 1.4 Test markers
- `unit`
- `integration`
- `safety`
- `slow`

### 1.5 Coverage targets
- `schemas/`: 100% line coverage
- `risk/controller.py`: 100% branch coverage
- `tools/backtest_tools.py`: 95%+ line coverage
- `memory/`: 90%+ line coverage
- `agents/`: 80%+ line coverage
- `orchestrator/`: 85%+ line coverage
- `api/`: 80%+ line coverage

