## 15) Priority Matrix

Priority 0 (must pass every commit):
- settings safety defaults
- risk gate enforcement
- paper/live trading safeguards
- backtest determinism and reward non-NaN
- strategy parse/retry guards

Priority 1 (must pass before release):
- all schema constraints
- memory consistency + concurrency
- orchestrator approval/rejection/refinement flows
- API contract consistency

Priority 2 (continuous hardening):
- extended integration stress scenarios
- advanced semantic retrieval quality
- performance optimization above thresholds

